## Acceptance contract inspected before live action

The plan requires an existing real two-host stream, an exactly 15-second network
interruption, and resumption within 20 seconds after restoration through a fresh,
strictly-greater `session_id` observed in real Ack traffic. The server must remain
Streaming and capture must not be restarted. The interruption mechanism must be
reverted and verified afterward.

Codegraph inspection of the current implementation returned these exact timers and
state rules:

- Client `HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL = 5s`, `RECONNECT_RETRY_INTERVAL = 5s`,
  `START_ACK_TIMEOUT = 5s`, and `MAX_MISSED_HEARTBEATS = 2`.
- Client `mark_unreachable` schedules the next retry five seconds later;
  `issue_start` mints a new session ID for every retry.
- Server `HEARTBEAT_TIMEOUT = 30s`; `handle_start` accepts only a strictly newer
  `SessionOrder` ID, changes `last_active_session_id`, and leaves capture running
  when already `Streaming`.

